name: sim.interpolatePoses
description: Computes the interpolated pose between poseIn1 and poseIn2
luaSynopsis: list resultPose = sim.interpolatePoses(list poseIn1, list poseIn2, float interpolFactor)
pythonSynopsis: float[7] resultPose = sim.interpolatePoses(float[7] poseIn1, float[7] poseIn2, float interpolFactor)
inputs:
1. poseIn1: first input pose (array of 7 values [x y z qx qy qz qw])
2. poseIn2: second input pose (array of 7 values [x y z qx qy qz qw])
3. interpolFactor: interpolation factor, a value between 0.0 and 1.0 (0.0--> resultPose = poseIn1, 1.0--> resultPose = poseIn2)
outputs:
1. resultPose: the result pose (array of 7 values [x y z qx qy qz qw])
